From 8920cef412f2a9893a12bc4d4fbc3147c8e0e2be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WhiskyTangoFox <aikimiller@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:54:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fo4 ObjectTemplate: restore OBTF, FULL, OBTS registration
 order

Mutagen 0.54.0 (commit aa7cc540e, "Standardize RecordType ordering")
alphabetized ObjectTemplate_Registration.AllRecordTypes to
(FULL, OBTF, OBTS). PluginBinaryOverlay.ParseRecordLocationsInternal
starts a new list item whenever trigger.AllRecordTypes.IndexOf(recType)
fails to strictly increase; on-disk FO4 ObjectTemplate subrecord order
is OBTF, FULL, OBTS, so under the alphabetized indices (FULL=0, OBTF=1,
OBTS=2) the OBTF(1)->FULL(0) transition looks like a decrease and the
lazy overlay reader (Fallout4ModBinaryOverlay) splits every on-disk
template in two. The deep parse (Fallout4Mod.CreateFromBinary) never
consults this ordering and is unaffected.

This is an isolated backport of commit 6aa769dab8e8bd50d488966a5c942ae3dd197c25
("Reverted record type ordering", 2026-07-07, first released in 0.54.2)
for this one file only -- confirmed identical to that commit's change here
via 'git diff 0.54.0 6aa769dab~1 -- <this file>' (empty: no other commit
touched this file between the regression and the revert).

MEditService issue #385.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../Records/Common Subrecords/ObjectTemplate_Generated.cs       | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Mutagen.Bethesda.Fallout4/Records/Common Subrecords/ObjectTemplate_Generated.cs b/Mutagen.Bethesda.Fallout4/Records/Common Subrecords/ObjectTemplate_Generated.cs
index ece97db8b..39b053b0f 100644
--- a/Mutagen.Bethesda.Fallout4/Records/Common Subrecords/ObjectTemplate_Generated.cs	
+++ b/Mutagen.Bethesda.Fallout4/Records/Common Subrecords/ObjectTemplate_Generated.cs	
@@ -578,8 +578,8 @@ namespace Mutagen.Bethesda.Fallout4
         private static readonly Lazy<RecordTriggerSpecs> _recordSpecs = new Lazy<RecordTriggerSpecs>(() =>
         {
             var all = RecordCollection.Factory(
-                RecordTypes.FULL,
                 RecordTypes.OBTF,
+                RecordTypes.FULL,
                 RecordTypes.OBTS);
             return new RecordTriggerSpecs(allRecordTypes: all);
         });
